<!--
  The mark, in one colour.

  Android tints a notification's small icon and a themed launcher icon to a
  single colour, so whatever is here becomes a silhouette whether it was drawn
  as one or not. The painted cat has no such form — traced faithfully it
  reduces to a blob, and simplified until the fur stops being noise it loses
  the ears, which are the only thing saying "cat" at twenty-four density
  pixels. So this is the cat *drawn for this size*: pointed ears, the raised
  paw held clear of the head with a gap wide enough to survive, and the coin
  punched out of the belly rather than struck onto it.

  The paw stands apart on purpose. Attached, at this size, it closes up into
  the head and the cat stops beckoning — which is the whole gesture.

  One path, evenOdd, so the coin is a hole rather than a shape that has to be
  painted a second colour it will not be allowed to keep.
-->
